---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Now" description="A short snapshot of what I’m doing right now.">
  <div class="page-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">Now</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">What I’m doing now</h1>
    <p class="page-lede">
      A short snapshot of the things taking up my attention. Updated November 2026.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="prose page-prose">
    <h2>Building</h2>
    <p>
      This site, mostly. I’m slowly learning how little a personal website needs: a few files,
      a good typeface, and somewhere to put the words.
    </p>

    <h2>Reading</h2>
    <p>
      A few books on typography and slow software, plus far too many tabs about static site
      generators. I keep coming back to the same idea: the best tools disappear.
    </p>

    <h2>Thinking about</h2>
    <p>
      The difference between a page that is minimal and a page that is merely empty. Restraint
      is a material, not an absence.
    </p>

    <h2>Uses</h2>
    <p>
      Astro and MDX for the site, a plain text editor for the words, and GitHub Pages for the
      hosting. The typefaces are Newsreader and Inter. Everything else is a browser and a
      terminal.
    </p>

    <p>
      <em>
        This page is inspired by <a href="https://nownownow.com">nownownow.com</a>.
      </em>
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
